  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Madan Anurath Vaidya And Another vs The State Of Maharashtra on 26 September, 2022 Author: S. G. Mehare Bench: S. G. Mehare 1 13-ABA.1281-22.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad 13 Anticipatory Bail Application No.1281 Of 2022 1. Madan Anurath Vaidya 2. Sudam Babasaheb Katule Versus The State Of Maharashtra ... Advocate for Applicants : Mr. Kawade Shrikant G. App for Respondent-State : Mr. V. M. Kagne. ... Coram : S. G. Mehare, J. Date : 26.09.2022 Per Court :- 1.",
    "facts": "They have been falsely implicated in the crime at Madan Anurath Vaidya And Another vs The State Of Maharashtra on 26 September, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/81606942/ 1 belated stage of the investigation. The offence under Section 328 of the IPC does not apply in the case at hand. The other offences are bailable. It is the case of transporting the scented Gutka and Pan Masala. The issue regarding the applicability of Section 328 of the IPC, is seized with the Hon'ble Apex Court. The names of the applicants have been disclosed at belated stage. Hence, the following order : ORDER (i) In the event of arrest, applicant Nos.1. MADAN ANURATH VAIDYA and 2. SUDAM BABASAHEB KATULE be released on interim bail, on furnishing P.B. and S.B. of Rs.20,000/- (Rupees Twenty Thousand only) each with one solvent surety of the like amount each, in Crime No.252 of 2022, registered with Police Station Murum, District Osmanabad, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273 and 328 of the IPC and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, on the conditions that they shall not tamper with the prosecution witnesses, they shall co-operate with the Investigating Officer. (S. G. MEHARE, J.) ... vmk/- Madan Anurath Vaidya And Another vs The State Of Maharashtra on 26 September, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/81606942/ 2",
